        "main": "x(t)=\\begin{cases}1,& |t|<T\\\\0,& \\text{otherwise}\\end{cases},\\quad \\text{bound the effective bandwidth of }x(t)*x(t)"
      },
      "final_answer": {
        "main": "B_\\omega\\ge \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{4T}\\quad \\text{for }y(t)=x(t)*x(t)\\text{ using }T_d=\\sqrt{\\frac25}T"
      },
      "solution_steps": [
        {
          "step": 1,
          "text": "The convolution of two width-2T rectangular pulses is a triangle: y(t)=x(t)*x(t)=2T-|t| for |t|<2T, and 0 otherwise."
        },
        {
          "step": 2,
          "text": "Use effective duration T_d=[∫t²|y(t)|²dt / ∫|y(t)|²dt]^{1/2}."
        },
        {
          "step": 3,
          "text": "Because y(t) is even, denominator D=2∫_0^{2T}(2T-t)^2dt=16T^3/3."
        },
        {
          "step": 4,
          "text": "Numerator N=2∫_0^{2T}t^2(2T-t)^2dt=32T^5/15."
        },
        {
          "step": 5,
          "text": "Thus T_d^2=N/D=(32T^5/15)/(16T^3/3)=2T^2/5, so T_d=√(2/5)T."
        },
        {
          "step": 6,
          "text": "Uncertainty principle: T_dB_ω≥1/2, hence B_ω≥1/(2T_d)=√10/(4T)."
        }
      ],
